Description:

backupcyrusd now works with directory-based cyrusdb backends such as zeroskip.
Message annotations are fetched per message with the new FANNOT command; FMETA
still sends the raw per-mailbox annotations database when asked, for older
clients.  The seen and subscription databases are sent as JSON objects of their
keys and values, whatever their backend.


Documentation:

The protocol is described in comments in imap/backupcyrusd.c.


Config changes:

None.


Upgrade instructions:

Upgrade backupcyrusd before the Cyrus::Backup client: older clients keep
working against the new server, but the new client needs FANNOT.  Don't move
annotation_db, seenstate_db or subscription_db to zeroskip until both are
upgraded.  Once the server is upgraded, backups store seen and sub in their
JSON form, whichever client takes them.

The backup state version is now 7; older states gain the new indexed.modseq
column on their next backup.  The first time each folder changes after that,
the client fetches annotations for all its messages and removes the folder's
raw cyrus.annotations file from the backup.


GitHub issue:

None.
